```
Need createWorld accept opts, but unnecessary if we set sun shadow after? World doesn't expose sun. Add `world.sun = sun` and maybe world.isSoftware? Could modify world options. Simpler: after createWorld, change sun shadow map size if expose. Add `world.sun = sun` in world. Set in main:
```
if (softwareRenderer) { world.sun.shadow.mapSize.set(1024,1024); renderer.shadowMap.autoUpdate=false; }
```
But shadow map may already have been created? No render yet. okay.

Would antialias still cost? yes. Could detect software before creating renderer via a probe. But let's first test with DPR 0.65, merged and shadows maybe. We can set antialias false if software through probe. Let's do probe function before renderer:

```
function detectSoftwareRenderer() {
 try {
 const probe=document.createElement('canvas')
 const gl=probe.getContext('webgl2') || probe.getContext('webgl')
 ...
 const lose = gl.getExtension('WEBGL_lose_context'); lose?.loseContext()
 return /.../.test(name)
